{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_hwx6ghxcmwyroo7pmsvbwc3v6yd2g4rmje5y5g7gtfmovh64dprq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Verification is complete. Here's what happened.\n\n## Setup\n\n`c_src/src/lib.c` is an inlined copy of `stb_ds.h` plus `strkey`/`arr_del`. `include/lib.h` declares only `void arr_del(int)`, but the `.so` exports **16** symbols — the whole hash-map/dynamic-array/string-arena machinery. All 16 are the verification surface.\n\n`cargo check` was clean from the start, and all 16 symbols were already exported by the Rust `.so` (0 missing).\n\n## Artifacts (Phase A)\n\n- **`SYMBOLS.md`** — 16/16 symbols, 0 missing, 0 extra, plus the 7 `static` C helpers and how each is reached.\n- **`ERRORS.md`** — 54 rows: every `return -1`/`return 0`/early `return a`, all seven `STBDS_ASSERT`s, every null/range check, both arena min/max constants.\n- **`CONFIGS.md`** — 83 rows over the real branch axes (`mode`, `table->string.mode`, the 4 map-creation entry points, `elemsize`/`keysize` shapes, grow/shrink/rebuild, probe path, delete position, hash-length classes, arena block growth).\n\n## Tests: 85, all through `libloading` on **both** `.so`s\n\n`tests/common/mod.rs` mirrors the C structs so `DualMap` compares the *complete* observable state — header, all hash-index counters, **every** bucket slot, **every** element — after every single operation, with fixed-seed randomized inputs.\n\n## Bugs found — in the translation, and in my own harness\n\n1. **Rust dropped the C's `assert()`s.** The C `.so` is built with `C_FLAGS = -fPIC` and **no `-DNDEBUG`**, so all seven `STBDS_ASSERT`s are live. The translation had commented them out, so for out-of-contract inputs C aborted while Rust silently continued. Fixed in `src/lib.rs`; `tests/crash_parity.rs` now confirms C and Rust die with the same signal in 11 fault/abort cases.\n\n2. **Harness: parallel tests raced on the libraries' global `stbds_hash_seed`.** Fixed with a process-wide lock.\n\n3. **Harness: `cargo test` does not rebuild a `cdylib`-only lib target** — I spent a while chasing a \"divergence\" that was a stale `.so`. `run_all.sh` now builds first, and the harness *refuses to run* if the `.so` is older than `src/lib.rs`.\n\n## Sensitivity check\n\nI didn't trust \"all green\", so I injected 29 deliberate bugs (`mutation-testing/`). 24 caught; the 5 survivors are each shown to be provably equivalent mutants (e.g. `ALIGN_FWD`'s argument is always `≡ 8 (mod 16)`, so `(n+a-1)` and `(n+a)` can never differ).\n\nThat run exposed a **real coverage gap**: the multi-bucket probe walk (`pos += step; step += 8`), present in three functions, needs two *consecutive* full 8-slot buckets — unreachable at ≤75% load. `tests/probe_paths.rs` now hand-builds bucket arrays byte-identically in both maps to force 2+ hops through all three copies (+ tombstone reuse, + wrap-around duplicates), with a watchdog so a diverging loop aborts in 30s instead of hanging.\n\n## Result\n\n```\n<default>               : 85 tests passed    symbol diff: EMPTY\n--no-default-features   : 85 tests passed    symbol diff: EMPTY\n--all-features          : 85 tests passed    symbol diff: EMPTY\n```\n\n`arr_del` deserves one caveat: it returns `void`, frees everything it allocates, and touches no global, so the only property that *can* be checked is \"doesn't fault or corrupt the heap\". Every genuinely untestable branch (e.g. `if (hash < 2)`, needing a 64-bit hash of exactly 0/1) is listed with its justification in `CONFIGS.md`; nothing was checked off on the strength of inspection alone without saying so."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":821,"cache_read_input_tokens":369798,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":821,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d19d6b00-8016-48f3-b947-3e7f2b4709b0","uuid":"7897eb60-15d9-466d-b053-8fdf0d3c7b06","timestamp":"2026-08-27T05:19:32.044Z"}
