et arrays byte-identically in both maps to force 2+ hops through all three copies (+ tombstone reuse, + wrap-around duplicates), with a watchdog so a diverging loop aborts in 30s instead of hanging.\n\n## Result\n\n```\n<default>               : 85 tests passed    symbol diff: EMPTY\n--no-default-features   : 85 tests passed    symbol diff: EMPTY\n--all-features          : 85 tests passed    symbol diff: EMPTY\n```\n\n`arr_del` deserves one caveat: it returns `void`, frees everything it allocates, and touches no global, so the only property that *can* be checked is \"doesn't fault or corrupt the heap\". Every genuinely untestable branch (e.g. `if (hash < 2)`, needing a 64-bit hash of exactly 0/1) is listed with its justification in `CONFIGS.md`; nothing was checked off on the strength of inspection alone without saying so.","ttft_ms":2727,"ttft_stream_ms":2519,"time_to_request_ms":50,"type":"result","duration_ms":4767365,"uuid":"62acbf7a-a166-44d2-923c-8f6618c480d0","queued_turn_count":0}
